---
permalink: /admin/make-commands/index.html
sitemap: false
---
{% extends "admin-layout.njk" %}
{% set pageTitle = "Make Commands | AFPD Admin" %}
{% set adminSection = "make-commands" %}
{% macro panel(id, title, commands) %}
<div class="command-panel">
  <div class="command-panel-heading"><span>{{ title }}</span><button type="button" class="command-copy" data-copy-target="{{ id }}" aria-label="Copy commands: {{ title }}" hidden>Copy</button></div>
  <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="{{ title }} commands"><code id="{{ id }}">{{ commands }}</code></pre>
  <p class="command-copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
</div>
{% endmacro %}
{% block pageAssets %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/admin-make-commands.css">
<script src="/js/admin-make-commands.js" defer></script>
{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<div class="admin-page-heading">
  <p class="commands-eyebrow">Admin database sync</p>
  <h1>Make Commands</h1>
  <p>Keep the admin database, source JSON and Git in sync. Choose your task, then work through its numbered panels. Copy each panel with the button in its upper-right corner.</p>
</div>
<aside class="commands-intro" aria-label="Before running commands">
  <h2>Before you start</h2>
  <p>Run these commands in your local <code>afpd-tracker</code> repository. Start with a clean working tree and save browser edits first. Pause when a step says to edit or review files. The <code>&amp;&amp;</code> between commands stops a copied panel if a command fails; stop the workflow and resolve that failure before continuing.</p>
  <p>Working database commands always use <strong>staging</strong> and accept no database parameter. <code>calls-from-db</code> saves transcripts; <code>evidence-from-db</code> saves evidence reviews. Download saved admin edits before uploading JSON to the database. A Git push saves files in the repository; it does not upload them to the admin database.</p>
</aside>
<nav class="command-task-nav" aria-label="Choose a task">
  {% for workflow in commandWorkflows %}<a href="#{{ workflow.id }}"{% if workflow.production %} class="command-production-link"{% endif %}>{{ workflow.title }}</a>{% endfor %}
  <a href="#command-reference">Database Make commands</a>
</nav>
<div class="command-workflows">
{% for workflow in commandWorkflows %}
  <details id="{{ workflow.id }}" class="command-workflow{% if workflow.production %} command-production{% endif %}"{% if workflow.open %} open{% endif %}>
    <summary>{% if workflow.production %}<span class="command-production-badge">Production</span>{% endif %}<span>{{ workflow.title }}</span></summary>
    <div class="command-workflow-body">
      <p class="command-summary">{{ workflow.summary }}</p>
      <ol class="command-steps">
      {% for step in workflow.steps %}
        <li><h2>{{ step.title }}</h2>{% if step.note %}<p>{{ step.note }}</p>{% endif %}
        {{ panel(workflow.id ~ "-step-" ~ loop.index, step.title, step.commands) }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </details>
{% endfor %}
</div>
<section id="command-reference" class="command-reference" aria-labelledby="command-reference-heading">
  <h2 id="command-reference-heading">Database Make commands</h2>
  <p>Only the admin database commands are listed here. Their descriptions come directly from the Makefile. Use the workflows above for the full download, upload and Git sequence.</p>
  <div class="command-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Command</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  {% for command in makeCommands %}<tr><th scope="row"><code>make {{ command.name }}</code></th><td>{{ command.description }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>
</section>
{% endblock %}
